From 70545ed1f2e903a2d3a5e2c454a2db20ec695d22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:58:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Kanban sync heal: a park lands where its own event
 recorded it

Review t_01a1cf75bc1d8e4c of PR1381 found three paths the heal got wrong:

- A kanban_continue wait (run outcome `continued`) was healed to todo and
  re-dispatched before its wake. `continued` is now a park; it lands the
  `status` its own event recorded (scheduled), and a no-wait continue that
  went straight back to ready falls through to todo.
- A review reopened to ready writes `review_reopened` with no payload, so
  the heal put the card back in review. `_LEFT_PARK` now carries every
  `kanban_resume_exec._LIFECYCLE_KINDS` move (review_reopened, triage_swept,
  gave_up, reclaimed, status); claimed/spawned open a new run, so they
  never reach this heal.
- An exhausted-budget block writes a `blocked` event but lands triage.
  block_task now records `status` (where the block landed) in the event
  payload, and the heal prefers it; older events fall back to the
  continuation_exhausted / goal_unachievable re-kind. A metadata_only
  `blocked` event (human-request migration re-filing an ask) is no move.

Non-blocking review nits: a non-v7 uid no longer reorders same-second
events, and a restored blocked ask re-syncs its resolved_check probe row.
